{"id":"phantastes-en_sct14_f2","schemaVersion":1,"fragmentId":"sha1:1fbfbb9f9deb27d2b8c8b7a1d27b212c48dcff57","generationHash":"sha1:2ce838f72dd8f7e4a44313aa3b8aeacb4b620d53","title":"Phantastes - VIII (Fragment 2)","text":"“Where is he?” I said, in some alarm, to the woman, who still sat reading.\n\n“There, on the floor, behind you,” she said, pointing with her arm half-outstretched, but not lifting her eyes. I turned and looked, but saw nothing. Then with a feeling that there was yet something behind me, I looked round over my shoulder; and there, on the ground, lay a black shadow, the size of a man. It was so dark, that I could see it in the dim light of the lamp, which shone full upon it, apparently without thinning at all the intensity of its hue.\n\n“I told you,” said the woman, “you had better not look into that closet.”\n\n“What is it?” I said, with a growing sense of horror.\n\n“It is only your shadow that has found you,” she replied. “Everybody’s shadow is ranging up and down looking for him. I believe you call it by a different name in your world: yours has found you, as every person’s is almost certain to do who looks into that closet, especially after meeting one in the forest, whom I dare say you have met.”\n\nHere, for the first time, she lifted her head, and looked full at me: her mouth was full of long, white, shining teeth; and I knew that I was in the house of the ogre. I could not speak, but turned and left the house, with the shadow at my heels. “A nice sort of valet to have,” I said to myself bitterly, as I stepped into the sunshine, and, looking over my shoulder, saw that it lay yet blacker in the full blaze of the sunlight. Indeed, only when I stood between it and the sun, was the blackness at all diminished. I was so bewildered⁠—stunned⁠—both by the event itself and its suddenness, that I could not at all realize to myself what it would be to have such a constant and strange attendance; but with a dim conviction that my present dislike would soon grow to loathing, I took my dreary way through the wood.","meta":{"bookId":"phantastes-en","bookTitle":"Phantastes","bookLanguage":"en","author":"George MacDonald","seriesId":"george-macdonald","seriesTitle":"George MacDonald","sectionIndex":14,"sectionTitle":"VIII","fragmentIndex":2,"fragmentsInSection":2,"sourceFile":"text/chapter-8.xhtml","stats":{"wordCount":348,"uniqueWordCount":195,"paragraphCount":6,"vocabularyCount":110,"levelDistribution":{"A1":35,"A2":24,"B1":27,"B2":17,"C1":7,"C2":0}}},"vocabulary":[{"word":"alarm","lemma":"alarm","lemmaId":"alarm","pos":"noun","source":"word","wordKey":"alarm_noun","level":"B2","translations":{"de":{"translation":"beunruhigt"},"es":{"translation":"alarmado"},"ru":{"translation":"тревога"},"uk":{"translation":"стривожений"}},"_spacyLemma":"alarm","exampleStart":26,"exampleEnd":36,"matchedForm":"alarm","levelSource":"vocabulary_index","ipa":"əˈlɑːm","difficultyScore":0.637143,"difficultySource":"zipf"},{"word":"apparently","lemma":"apparently","lemmaId":"apparently","pos":"adverb","source":"word","wordKey":"apparently_adverb","level":"B2","translations":{"de":{"translation":"anscheinend"},"es":{"translation":"aparentemente"},"ru":{"translation":"по всей видимости"},"uk":{"translation":"помітно"}},"_spacyLemma":"apparently","exampleStart":476,"exampleEnd":535,"matchedForm":"apparently","levelSource":"vocabulary_index","ipa":"əˈpærəntli","difficultyScore":0.488571,"difficultySource":"zipf"},{"word":"arm","lemma":"arm","lemmaId":"arm","pos":"noun","source":"word","wordKey":"arm_noun","level":"A1","translations":{"ru":{"translation":"руки"},"uk":{"translation":"руку"}},"_spacyLemma":"arm","exampleStart":135,"exampleEnd":142,"matchedForm":"arm","levelSource":"vocabulary_index","ipa":"ɑːm","difficultyScore":0.508571,"difficultySource":"zipf"},{"word":"attendance","lemma":"attendance","lemmaId":"attendance","pos":"noun","source":"word","wordKey":"attendance_noun","level":"A2","translations":{"ru":{"translation":"посещаемост